From 14d513beb9c27de74821e68e34c6f53f6aad8218 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jiafei Pan <Jiafei.Pan@nxp.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Apr 2026 14:11:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 12/13] bl31: add multicore fastboot support

Multicore Fastboot is a Heterogeneous Multicore feature for MPU platform.
Currently BL31 could only boot non Secure image from master CPU Core, this
feature is to enable BL31 to boot multiple nonsecure images on multiple
secondary CPU Cores except master CPU Core.

In order to use this feature, firstly need to embedded a fastboot entry
blob in master Core's nonsecure image at offset defined by
NS_IMAGE_FASTBOOT_OFFSET, then bl31 will check whether a valid fastboot
entry blob is available, if yes, then parse the boot entry information
from blob and then start it from specific CPU Core.

Signed-off-by: Jiafei Pan <Jiafei.Pan@nxp.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
